# 9 Articles of Development (Immutable)

| Article | Principle | Description |
|:--------|:----------|:------------|
| **I** | **Library-First** | Build logic as standalone libraries/modules first. |
| **II** | **CLI Interface** | Expose core logic via CLI for easy testing. |
| **III** | **Test-First** | **NON-NEGOTIABLE**: Write tests before implementation. |
| **IV** | **Pure Functions** | Prefer pure functions over stateful classes. |
| **V** | **Standard Libs** | Use standard libraries whenever possible. |
| **VI** | **Single File** | Keep related logic in one file until it exceeds 500 lines. |
| **VII** | **Simplicity** | Avoid complex abstractions. Write for readability. |
| **VIII** | **Anti-Abstraction** | Use frameworks directly. Don't hide them. |
| **IX** | **Integration** | Test with real components (DB, API) over mocks. |
